    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108260" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποδέξιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποδέχομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>able to
				receive, capacious, ample,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμένες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.49
				</span></i>
			; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποδοχεύς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				364
			</span></i> (lyr.), for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποδεξίαις
			ἁμίλλαις</span> (codd.) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδεξίοις</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποδεξιᾶν</span> are conjectured.</div>
